⚡🇺🇸🇩🇪The 2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine was awarded to American neuroscientist Karl Deisseroth and German biophysicists Peter Hegemann and Georg Nagel for their discoveries on light-activated ion channels and the development of optogenetics.

In short, they contributed to developing a kind of "light switch" for neurons: by genetically modifying certain cells, it is possible to make them react to light and thus activate or inhibit them with great precision, in order to study how the brain works.

